{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וסמך לו ולא תחמוד", :translit "ve-samach lo ve-lo tachmod", :gloss "and its juxtaposition: and you shall not covet"} {:he "שלא יחמוד אשת חבירו", :translit "she-lo yachmod eshet chavero", :gloss "that one not covet his fellow's wife"} {:he "ויעיד בו עדות שקר לומר שמת כדי שישאנה", :translit "ve-ya'id bo edut sheker lomar she-met kedey she-yis'ena", :gloss "and testify against him false testimony to say that he died in order to marry her"} {:he "ושדהו", :translit "u-sdeho", :gloss "and his field"} {:he "הוסיף כאן שכבר הגיעו קרוב לארץ והיה להם שדות", :translit "hosif kan she-kvar higi'u karov la-aretz ve-haya lahem sadot", :gloss "added here, for they had already drawn near to the land and they had fields"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): the verse sequence of 'you shall not covet' next to 'you shall not bear false witness' warns that covetous desire can drive one to perjury."} {:kind :other, :note "Plural 'fields' in Deuteronomy 5:21 versus singular 'field' in Exodus 20:14 reflects Israel's new proximity to the land."}], :frame {:text "The Decalogue in Deuteronomy 5:18–19 lists 'you shall not covet' (ולא תחמוד) immediately after 'you shall not bear false witness' (ולא תענה), a sequence the Ba'al HaTurim reads as causally linked. The parallel verse in Exodus 20:14 reads 'your fellow's wife' without mention of a field; Deuteronomy 5:21 adds 'and his field' (ושדהו), reflecting that Israel stood about to enter and inherit the land.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 5:18" "Deuteronomy 5:19" "Exodus 20:14" "Exodus 20:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): the verse sequence of 'you shall not covet' next to 'you shall not bear false witness' warns that covetous desire can drive one to perjury.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Plural 'fields' in Deuteronomy 5:21 versus singular 'field' in Exodus 20:14 reflects Israel's new proximity to the land.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:39.238934093Z", :model "glm-5.2"}